      "text": "A selective calendar of events, meetings, and public life around White Plains.\n\nEvents\n\nUpcoming\n\nEvents most likely to matter to White Plains residents.\n\nDowntown White Plains Rock the Block 2026\n\nMay 20, 2026 - Aug 19, 2026\n\nDowntown summer street music and dining on Mamaroneck Avenue.\n\nAnastasia: Youth Edition\n\nJun 29, 2026 - Jul 18, 2026\n\nAnastasia: The Musical is the spectacular new musical about discovering who you are and defining who you’re meant to be.\n\nArtificial Intelligence (A.I.) in the Igloo\n\nJul 8, 2026\n\nLearn about the current state of Artificial Intelligence (A.I.) and some of the exciting possibilities.\n\nDigital Decluttering\n\nJul 8, 2026\n\nIn this workshop, we'll slow down and actually understand why digital chaos builds up - and what to do about it.\n\nSoccer Fest: Family Movie Night: Air Bud World Pup (2001)\n\nJul 9, 2026\n\nSoccer Fest: Family Movie Night: Air Bud World Pup (2001) in White Plains. Details are available from the City.\n\nEarring Making Workshop\n\nJul 10, 2026\n\nJoan Lloyd donates hundreds of pairs of beaded earrings every year to women's shelters.\n\nWhite Plains Soccer Fest\n\nJul 11, 2026\n\nA downtown fan festival and block party on Mamaroneck Avenue with family-friendly activities.\n\nSoccer Fest: Watch Party\n\nJul 11, 2026\n\nSoccer Fest: Watch Party in White Plains. Details are available from the City.\n\nNeighborhood Nights\n\nJul 13, 2026\n\nNeighborhood Nights at Thomas H. Slater Center. Details are available from the City.\n\nDestination College Workshop Series\n\nJul 13, 2026\n\nWorkshop 10: Beyond the Application (Interviews, Portfolios & Professionalism) Focus: Presenting yourself with confidence and authenticity.\n\nUnearth a Story\n\nJul 14, 2026\n\nJoin us for Unearth a Story, a generative writing workshop designed to help participants uncover the stories inside you!\n\nWestchester During Revolutionary War (History via Igloo)\n\nJul 15, 2026\n\nLearn about Westchester County during the Revolutionary War and what happened throughout the conflict.\n\nJuly 15 — Downtown White Plains Rock the Block\n\nJul 15, 2026\n\nDowntown summer street music and dining on Mamaroneck Avenue.\n\nSpies in Disguise: Zoom Virtual Program\n\nJul 15, 2026\n\nFrom the birth of our nation, women have served alongside men, helping to create the United States of Am erica during the Am erican Revolution.\n\nComité Noviembre: Reception\n\nJul 16, 2026\n\nThe evening will feature an intimate discussion with Chairwoman Teresa Santiago, accompanied by featured artists, music, light bites, and refreshments.\n\nSchool Of Rock: Young Actors\n\nJul 20, 2026 - Aug 8, 2026\n\nAndrew Lloyd Webber’s School of Rock: Young Actors Edition is a dynamic, one-hour version of the musical based on the hit movie.\n\nNeighborhood Nights\n\nJul 20, 2026\n\nNeighborhood Nights at Delfino Park."
