      "type": "event",
      "excerpt": "It&#39;s Am erica&#39;s 250th birthday, and for researchers across the country, Revolutionary War Pensions offer up valuable information about a veteran&#39;s life,…",
      "text": "It&#39;s Am erica&#39;s 250th birthday, and for researchers across the country, Revolutionary War Pensions offer up valuable information about a veteran&#39;s life,…\n\nLearning\n\nAm erica 250: The Importance of Revolutionary War Pensions\n\nIt's Am erica's 250th birthday, and for researchers across the country, Revolutionary War Pensions offer up valuable information about a veteran's life,…\n\nAbout this event\n\nIt's Am erica's 250th birthday, and for researchers across the country, Revolutionary War Pensions offer up valuable information about a veteran's life, family, and service. This program shares how to find pensions, the information often available, and interpretation tips that are helpful to genealogists and researchers alike! Presented in collaboration with Ruth Keeler Memorial Library, White Plains Public Library, Eastchester Public Library and The Field Library. Registration is required. Click Here To Register. Click Here to Join the Zoom Directly. Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nPast\n\nDate\n\nTuesday, June 23, 2026\n\nTime\n\n7:00 PM - 8:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nWestchester During Revolutionary War (History via Igloo)\n\nMay 21, 2026\n\nLearn about Westchester County during the Revolutionary War and what happened throughout the conflict.\n\nRev250: Westchester County in the Am erican Revolution\n\nJun 11, 2026\n\nLocal historian Stephen Paul Devillo will discuss his latest book, Westchester County in the Am erican Revolution: Neutral Ground.\n\nCANCELED The Birth of NY in White Plains (History via Igloo)\n\nJun 16, 2026\n\nEVENT CANCELED"
