      "text": "The evening will feature an intimate discussion with Chairwoman Teresa Santiago, accompanied by featured artists, music, light bites, and refreshments.\n\nLearning\n\nComité Noviembre: Reception\n\nThe evening will feature an intimate discussion with Chairwoman Teresa Santiago, accompanied by featured artists, music, light bites, and refreshments.\n\nAbout this event\n\nThe evening will feature an intimate discussion with Chairwoman Teresa Santiago, accompanied by featured artists, music, light bites, and refreshments. The event is free but registration is required. Comit&eacute; Noviembre is a NY-based organization committed to preserving, honoring, and celebrating the deep cultural roots and lived experiences of the Puerto Rican diaspora in New York, across the U.S., and on the island. The exhibit will be on view in the Library's Museum Gallery through September 1. &iexcl;Que Viva Puerto Rico! Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nUpcoming\n\nDate\n\nThursday, July 16, 2026\n\nTime\n\n7:00 PM - 8:45 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nCitywide School Art Show\n\nMay 27, 2026\n\nReception Details: Church Street and George Washington Schools: Thursday, May 28 4:30-5:30pm Mamaroneck Avenue, Post Road and Ridgeway Schools: Tuesday, June 2,…\n\nCitywide School Art Show\n\nMay 28, 2026\n\nReception Details: Church Street and George Washington Schools: Thursday, May 28 4:30-5:30pm Mamaroneck Avenue, Post Road and Ridgeway Schools: Tuesday, June 2,…\n\nCitywide Art Show\n\nJun 5, 2026\n\nReception Details: Church Street and George Washington Schools: Thursday, May 28 Mamaroneck Avenue, Post Road and Ridgeway Schools: Tuesday, June 2 Eastview,…"
