      "text": "Introduction to Computers: Learn the Basics This beginner-friendly class is designed for those who are new to computers or looking to build confidence with…\n\nLearning\n\nComputer Basics: Introduction to Computers\n\nIntroduction to Computers: Learn the Basics This beginner-friendly class is designed for those who are new to computers or looking to build confidence with…\n\nAbout this event\n\nIntroduction to Computers: Learn the Basics This beginner-friendly class is designed for those who are new to computers or looking to build confidence with technology. Participants will learn how to use a mouse and keyboard, navigate a computer, and understand basic terminology. The class will also cover how to browse the internet, set up and use email, and practice essential skills for everyday use. No prior experience is needed. Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nPast\n\nDate\n\nThursday, May 28, 2026\n\nTime\n\n2:00 PM - 3:30 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nCreating a Compelling College Application this Summer\n\nMay 20, 2026\n\nProgram for High School Juniors: Creating a Compelling College Application this Summer We are offering this Zoom presentation to help high school juniors and…\n\nWestchester During Revolutionary War (History via Igloo)\n\nMay 21, 2026\n\nLearn about Westchester County during the Revolutionary War and what happened throughout the conflict.\n\nRev250: Westchester County in the Am erican Revolution\n\nJun 11, 2026\n\nLocal historian Stephen Paul Devillo will discuss his latest book, Westchester County in the Am erican Revolution: Neutral Ground."
