      "excerpt": "In this workshop, we&#39;ll slow down and actually understand why digital chaos builds up - and what to do about it.",
      "text": "In this workshop, we&#39;ll slow down and actually understand why digital chaos builds up - and what to do about it.\n\nWorkshop\n\nDigital Decluttering\n\nIn this workshop, we'll slow down and actually understand why digital chaos builds up - and what to do about it.\n\nAbout this event\n\nIn this workshop, we'll slow down and actually understand why digital chaos builds up - and what to do about it. You'll walk away with a clear framework, a few simple strategies to start right away, and a whole lot less dread about opening your laptop. Shannon Reilly is the founder of Simplify Space & Soul, a holistic wellness and organizing practice dedicated to helping people feel more at ease in their spaces, their schedules, and themselves. She holds certifications as a Professional Organizer (CPO, CVPO), Neurodiversity Coach, and Productivity Specialist, and has been teaching Therapeutic Yoga for over a decade. For more than ten years, Shannon has helped people cut through overwhelm - whether that shows up as a cluttered home, an overflowing inbox, a packed calendar, or just the feeling that life is moving too fast to catch up with. Her work is always customized, never judgmental, and rooted in the belief that small, sustainable changes make the biggest difference. This program takes place on Zoom and registration is required. Click here to register. The program is being presented in partnership with the Ruth Keeler Memorial Library and several other Westchester Libraries. Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nUpcoming\n\nDate\n\nWednesday, July 8, 2026\n\nTime\n\n7:00 PM - 8:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nDestination College Workshop Series\n\nJul 13, 2026\n\nWorkshop 10: Beyond the Application (Interviews, Portfolios & Professionalism) Focus: Presenting yourself with confidence and authenticity.\n\nUnearth a Story\n\nJul 14, 2026\n\nJoin us for Unearth a Story, a generative writing workshop designed to help participants uncover the stories inside you!\n\nPowerful Public Speaking & Presentation Skills\n\nJul 28, 2026\n\nWe will be hosting the following program in partnership with The College of Westchester This seminar is designed to help students overcome their fear of…"
