      "excerpt": "A Stonewall Book Award winner and finalist for the Pulitzer Prize and National Book Award, the novel is set in Chicago 1985 and Paris thirty years later and…",
      "text": "A Stonewall Book Award winner and finalist for the Pulitzer Prize and National Book Award, the novel is set in Chicago 1985 and Paris thirty years later and…\n\nLearning\n\nFuture is Female\n\nA Stonewall Book Award winner and finalist for the Pulitzer Prize and National Book Award, the novel is set in Chicago 1985 and Paris thirty years later and…\n\nAbout this event\n\nA Stonewall Book Award winner and finalist for the Pulitzer Prize and National Book Award, the novel is set in Chicago 1985 and Paris thirty years later and is described by The New York Times as \"A page-turner.an absorbing and emotionally riveting story about what it's like to live during times of crisis,\" a story of friendship, tragedy, and redemption. This book can be accessed through audio or ebook in Libby or in the Library's physical collection. To join, Click This Zoom Link. You can also use the following phone number to call in: +1 929 436 2866 US (New York). Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nPast\n\nDate\n\nMonday, June 1, 2026\n\nTime\n\n2:00 PM - 3:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nWhite Plains Sustainability Fair\n\nMay 16, 2026\n\nActivities: Make exploding wildflower seed balls Re-think eating and menus for healthier, sustainable food choices Watch composting demonstrations Learn about…\n\nWestchester During Revolutionary War (History via Igloo)\n\nMay 21, 2026\n\nLearn about Westchester County during the Revolutionary War and what happened throughout the conflict.\n\nCANCELED The Birth of NY in White Plains (History via Igloo)\n\nJun 16, 2026\n\nEVENT CANCELED"
