      "id": "page:/events/library-over-the-rainbow-and-through-the-woods-2026-05-17/",
      "sourceId": "page:/events/library-over-the-rainbow-and-through-the-woods-2026-05-17/",
      "title": "Over the Rainbow and Through the Woods",
      "url": "/events/library-over-the-rainbow-and-through-the-woods-2026-05-17/",
      "type": "event",
      "excerpt": "Pack your (imaginary) bags and join musical educator Rebecca Schoffer for a joyful, interactive sing-along celebrating Jewish Am erican Heritage Month!",
      "text": "Pack your (imaginary) bags and join musical educator Rebecca Schoffer for a joyful, interactive sing-along celebrating Jewish Am erican Heritage Month!\n\nLearning\n\nOver the Rainbow and Through the Woods\n\nPack your (imaginary) bags and join musical educator Rebecca Schoffer for a joyful, interactive sing-along celebrating Jewish Am erican Heritage Month!\n\nAbout this event\n\nPack your (imaginary) bags and join musical educator Rebecca Schoffer for a joyful, interactive sing-along celebrating Jewish Am erican Heritage Month! Travel through time with songs that journeyed across oceans and generations, from traditional Yiddish folk to Am erican classics, beloved children's music, and pop hits by Jewish Am erican songwriters. Families will clap, move, and sing together, as we explore how music tells stories of home, hope, and the Jewish Am erican experience. Recommended for families with children ages 0-8. ~~~~ Rebecca Schoffer is an experiential educator, musician, and community builder who travels to organizations around the world to lead joyful concerts and teach educator workshops. She serves as Director of Jewish Family Life and the leader of the beloved Shababa community at the 92nd Street Y. She is the founder and creative director of Glowhouse Studio, an independent production house. Her latest musical family film, FLAME, premiered in 2025. She is also a recording artist and singer-songwriter who has released multiple albums of Jewish family music, available everywhere you stream music. A graduate of the Atlantic Theater Conservatory and Tufts University, she is a playwright and director of family theater. She received the 2019 Young Pioneers Award for innovative educators. Learn more at: www. Rebecca Schoffer.com Connect on Instagram: @Rebecca Schoffer Music Watch on You Tube: https://www.youtube.com/@The Rebecca Show Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nPast\n\nDate\n\nSunday, May 17, 2026\n\nTime\n\n2:00 PM - 3:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nGet Moving!\n\nMay 11, 2026\n\nThrough playful literacy movement games, music, stretching, and creative activities, children will jump, wiggle, dance, and explore different ways their…\n\nSummer Reading Kickoff featuring Jumpin' Jamie!\n\nJun 27, 2026\n\nCome start your summer vacation at the White Plains Public Library!\n\nOver in the Meadow: VR Search and Find!\n\nMay 19, 2026\n\nExperience Virtual Reality (VR) without a headset in the Library's panoramic content room."
