      "text": "We will be hosting the following program in partnership with The College of Westchester What is YOUR personal brand saying about you?\n\nWorkshop\n\nWOW Factor: Developing Your Personal Brand\n\nWe will be hosting the following program in partnership with The College of Westchester What is YOUR personal brand saying about you?\n\nAbout this event\n\nWe will be hosting the following program in partnership with The College of Westchester What is YOUR personal brand saying about you? Participants will explore what a personal brand is, and how their experience, organizational skills, communication skills, dependability, ability to be a team player, and personal appearance all build personal brand. Students will also discover types of verbal and non-verbal communication and how body position and facial expressions can dictate how a message is received. Regardless of who you are, and what you are looking to do, you will have the skills and knowledge to be successful in any environment. Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nUpcoming\n\nDate\n\nWednesday, August 5, 2026\n\nTime\n\n6:00 PM - 7:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nPowerful Public Speaking & Presentation Skills\n\nJul 28, 2026\n\nWe will be hosting the following program in partnership with The College of Westchester This seminar is designed to help students overcome their fear of…\n\nResume Writing in the 21st Century\n\nAug 19, 2026\n\nWe will be hosting the following program in partnership with The College of Westchester Today's hiring process has evolved way beyond emailing resumes…\n\nOvercoming Ageism in the Workplace\n\nMay 13, 2026\n\nHow to protect your career or job search from age bias How to address ageism assumptions and myths."
